{
  "id": 529724088,
  "iid": 26435,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "KDP: Validate option length to prevent infinite loop",
  "description": "Summary:\n\nIn dissect_kdp(), option_len was read without verifying that it is at least 2 bytes. For option 6 and unknown options, offset is updated with (option_len - 2). If option_len is 0, the subtraction cancels previous increments, causing an infinite loop (DoS) or a negative item length exception.\n\nChanges:\n\n\\- Added a check ensuring option_len is at least 2 bytes before advancing offset.\n\n\\- Breaks out of the options loop if option_len is less than 2.\n\n\\- Verified with tools/check_apis.py (0 warnings).",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-09-09T04:43:26.797Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-09-10T17:47:41.355Z",
